@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ito-il29-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-il29-time`
IMPORT `ito-il29-published-figures`
IMPORT `ito-s2-2b-vehicle-value`
IMPORT `ito-s2-2b-phone-value`
IMPORT `ito-il29-test-people`
IMPORT `ito-s1-israeli-resident-individual`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Row IL-29 tests: s 2(2)(b), the value of the use of a vehicle (Regulations of 5747-1987 and 5776-2015) and of a mobile
-- telephone (Regulations of 5762-2002).  Every expected value was worked by hand from the Hebrew text before the code was
-- run; the arithmetic is in the comment beside it.  The NIS figures the Regulations leave to publication (the caps, the
-- adjusted reductions) are the published figures of ito-il29-published-figures.l4, not law.
-- ===========================================================================

`D` MEANS `the default readings of row IL-29`

GIVEN w   IS A NUMBER
      c08 IS A NUMBER
      c09 IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The facts that fix the rate of use value`
`the rate facts` w `with indices` c08 `and` c09 MEANS
    `The facts that fix the rate of use value` WITH
        `the weighted price in 2010 of models of class M1 or N1 first registered from 1 January to 30 September 2010` IS w
        `the consumer price index of November 2008` IS c08
        `the consumer price index of November 2009` IS c09

-- Rate facts that give 2.5% (W = 130,000, indices equal).
`F` MEANS `the rate facts` 130000 `with indices` 100 `and` 100

GIVEN cl    IS A `The class of a vehicle`
      dr    IS A `The drive of a vehicle`
      reg   IS A DATE
      price IS A NUMBER
      total IS A NUMBER
      days  IS A NUMBER
      itx   IS A NUMBER
      irx   IS A NUMBER
      avg   IS A NUMBER
      jan   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A vehicle put at an employee's disposal`
`a vehicle of class` cl `, drive` dr `, first registered` reg `, listed at` price `, daily prices` total `over` days `days, indices` itx `and` irx `, exchange rates` avg `and` jan MEANS
    `A vehicle put at an employee's disposal` WITH
        `a vehicle within the Vehicle Expenses Deduction Regulations of 5755-1995` IS TRUE
        `the class` IS cl
        `the drive` IS dr
        `first registered on` IS reg
        `the original price` IS `by the importer's price list` WITH `the price on the list, with the standard package, the mandatory accessories and the listed additions, with VAT, without promotion prices and discounts` IS price
        `the total of the daily consumer prices in the year of first registration` IS total
        `the number of days they are averaged over` IS days
        `the index known on 1 January of the tax year` IS itx
        `the index known on 1 January of the year of first registration` IS irx
        `the average exchange rate of the import currency in the year of first registration` IS avg
        `the exchange rate known on 1 January of the year of first registration` IS jan

`a car` MEANS `a private or light commercial vehicle of class M1 or N1`

-- A car whose daily price equals its listed price all year (total = 365 x price), the indices rising 5%, the rate flat.
GIVEN dr IS A `The drive of a vehicle`
      reg IS A DATE
      price IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A vehicle put at an employee's disposal`
`a flat-priced car with drive` dr `first registered` reg `at` price MEANS
    `a vehicle of class` `a car` `, drive` dr `, first registered` reg `, listed at` price `, daily prices` (price TIMES 365) `over` 365 `days, indices` 105 `and` 100 `, exchange rates` 3.6 `and` 3.6

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      v IS A `A vehicle put at an employee's disposal`
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-29`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`monthly` y v `under` r MEANS `s 2(2)(b) — the monthly value of the use of a vehicle in the tax year` y `, fixed by` `F` `, of` v `under` r

§ `The rate of use value (VEH reg 2(a))`

-- Band (1): W not above 123,000 -> 2.6%.  Bands (2) to (10): W x (Nov 2008 index) / (Nov 2009 index) above the lower and not
-- above the upper bound.  Indices equal here, so the adjusted figure is W.
#ASSERT `the rate of use value, fixed by` (`the rate facts` 100000 `with indices` 100 `and` 100) EQUALS 0.026
#ASSERT `the rate of use value, fixed by` (`the rate facts` 123000 `with indices` 100 `and` 100) EQUALS 0.026
#ASSERT `the rate of use value, fixed by` (`the rate facts` 123001 `with indices` 100 `and` 100) EQUALS 0.0258
#ASSERT `the rate of use value, fixed by` (`the rate facts` 124000 `with indices` 100 `and` 100) EQUALS 0.0258
#ASSERT `the rate of use value, fixed by` (`the rate facts` 124001 `with indices` 100 `and` 100) EQUALS 0.0256
#ASSERT `the rate of use value, fixed by` (`the rate facts` 125000 `with indices` 100 `and` 100) EQUALS 0.0256
#ASSERT `the rate of use value, fixed by` (`the rate facts` 125001 `with indices` 100 `and` 100) EQUALS 0.0254
#ASSERT `the rate of use value, fixed by` (`the rate facts` 126000 `with indices` 100 `and` 100) EQUALS 0.0254
#ASSERT `the rate of use value, fixed by` (`the rate facts` 126001 `with indices` 100 `and` 100) EQUALS 0.0252
#ASSERT `the rate of use value, fixed by` (`the rate facts` 127000 `with indices` 100 `and` 100) EQUALS 0.0252
#ASSERT `the rate of use value, fixed by` (`the rate facts` 127001 `with indices` 100 `and` 100) EQUALS 0.025
#ASSERT `the rate of use value, fixed by` (`the rate facts` 135000 `with indices` 100 `and` 100) EQUALS 0.025
#ASSERT `the rate of use value, fixed by` (`the rate facts` 135001 `with indices` 100 `and` 100) EQUALS 0.0248
#ASSERT `the rate of use value, fixed by` (`the rate facts` 136000 `with indices` 100 `and` 100) EQUALS 0.0248
#ASSERT `the rate of use value, fixed by` (`the rate facts` 136001 `with indices` 100 `and` 100) EQUALS 0.0246
#ASSERT `the rate of use value, fixed by` (`the rate facts` 137000 `with indices` 100 `and` 100) EQUALS 0.0246
#ASSERT `the rate of use value, fixed by` (`the rate facts` 137001 `with indices` 100 `and` 100) EQUALS 0.0244
#ASSERT `the rate of use value, fixed by` (`the rate facts` 138000 `with indices` 100 `and` 100) EQUALS 0.0244
#ASSERT `the rate of use value, fixed by` (`the rate facts` 138001 `with indices` 100 `and` 100) EQUALS 0.0243
-- Bands (2) to (10) use the multiplied figure: W = 137,000 x 101 / 100 = 138,370 -> above 138,000 -> 2.43% (band (10)),
-- where W alone would be band (8)/(9)'s 2.46%.
#ASSERT `the rate of use value, fixed by` (`the rate facts` 137000 `with indices` 101 `and` 100) EQUALS 0.0243
-- Band (1) uses W itself, not the multiplied figure: W = 120,000 with 100/110 is still band (1).
#ASSERT `the rate of use value, fixed by` (`the rate facts` 120000 `with indices` 100 `and` 110) EQUALS 0.026
-- A gap in the text: W = 123,500 is above 123,000 so band (1) fails; 123,500 x 100 / 110 = 112,272.7 is not above 123,000 so
-- bands (2) to (10) fail: no band.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the rate of use value, fixed by` (`the rate facts` 123500 `with indices` 100 `and` 110) BECAUSE "no band of the rate of use value fits: the weighted price in 2010 is above 123,000 but, multiplied by the November 2008 index and divided by the November 2009 index, it is not above 123,000 either, and the text prints no rate for it"

§ `The monthly value in the year of first registration`

-- Registered 10 Mar 2024, tax year 2024 (the year of registration): the adjusted consumer price is the original price (VEH
-- line 20).  200,000 x 2.5% = 5,000.
#ASSERT `monthly` 2024 (`a flat-priced car with drive` `an ordinary vehicle` `first registered` (YMD 2024 3 10) `at` 200000) `under` `D` EQUALS 5000
-- Rounding to the nearest multiple of 10: 200,500 x 2.5% = 5,012.5 -> 501.25 tens -> 5,010.
#ASSERT `monthly` 2024 (`a flat-priced car with drive` `an ordinary vehicle` `first registered` (YMD 2024 3 10) `at` 200500) `under` `D` EQUALS 5010
-- A midpoint: 200,200 x 2.5% = 5,005 -> 500.5 tens.  "הקרוב" does not say which of 5,000 and 5,010 (fork MP).
#ASSERT REFUSED `monthly` 2024 (`a flat-priced car with drive` `an ordinary vehicle` `first registered` (YMD 2024 3 10) `at` 200200) `under` `D` BECAUSE "the monthly value of the use of the vehicle is not settled: the allowed readings (a midpoint in rounding, the personal-import depreciation, the schedule a pre-2010 reduction refers to, a reduction larger than the value) give different amounts"
#ASSERT `monthly` 2024 (`a flat-priced car with drive` `an ordinary vehicle` `first registered` (YMD 2024 3 10) `at` 200200) `under` (`the defaults, except midpoint read` `a midpoint rounds up`) EQUALS 5010
#ASSERT `monthly` 2024 (`a flat-priced car with drive` `an ordinary vehicle` `first registered` (YMD 2024 3 10) `at` 200200) `under` (`the defaults, except midpoint read` `a midpoint rounds down`) EQUALS 5000
-- The cap on the adjusted consumer price: 2024 563,790.  570,000 is capped: 563,790 x 2.5% = 14,094.75 -> 1,409.475 tens -> 14,090.
#ASSERT `monthly` 2024 (`a flat-priced car with drive` `an ordinary vehicle` `first registered` (YMD 2024 3 10) `at` 570000) `under` `D` EQUALS 14090
-- 2026: cap 596,860.  600,000 is capped: 596,860 x 2.5% = 14,921.5 -> 1,492.15 tens -> 14,920.  596,860 itself is not above the cap: the same.
#ASSERT `monthly` 2026 (`a flat-priced car with drive` `an ordinary vehicle` `first registered` (YMD 2026 1 5) `at` 600000) `under` `D` EQUALS 14920
#ASSERT `monthly` 2026 (`a flat-priced car with drive` `an ordinary vehicle` `first registered` (YMD 2026 1 5) `at` 596860) `under` `D` EQUALS 14920
-- A vehicle of another class takes the same rule (reg 2(a): "ברכב, למעט אופנוע כאמור בתקנת משנה (ב)").
#ASSERT `monthly` 2024 (`a vehicle of class` `another vehicle, not of class M1, N1 or L3` `, drive` `an ordinary vehicle` `, first registered` (YMD 2024 3 10) `, listed at` 200000 `, daily prices` 0 `over` 365 `days, indices` 105 `and` 100 `, exchange rates` 3.6 `and` 3.6) `under` `D` EQUALS 5000

§ `The monthly value in a later year, with the reductions of the temporary provision`

-- Registered 1 Feb 2025, tax year 2026.  The daily price equals the original price all year (average 200,000), the exchange
-- rates are equal (the exchange ratio is not below 1: 1), the index ratio is 105 / 100 = 1.05.
--   adjustment difference: lower of (1) 200,000 - 200,000 = 0 and (2) 200,000 - 200,000 = 0 -> 0, below 1% of the original price,
--   so the adjusted price is 1.05 x 200,000 = 210,000 (under the cap 596,860); x 2.5% = 5,250 -> 5,250.
-- Reductions (VTP reg 1): a hybrid vehicle first registered from 1 Jan 2010: (c1) 580 in 2026 -> 4,670;
--   a plug-in: (d1) 1,150 -> 4,100 (and not (c1) as well: (e));   an electric vehicle: (d2) 1,380 -> 3,870.
#ASSERT `monthly` 2026 (`a flat-priced car with drive` `an ordinary vehicle` `first registered` (YMD 2025 2 1) `at` 200000) `under` `D` EQUALS 5250
#ASSERT `monthly` 2026 (`a flat-priced car with drive` `a hybrid vehicle` `first registered` (YMD 2025 2 1) `at` 200000) `under` `D` EQUALS 4670
#ASSERT `monthly` 2026 (`a flat-priced car with drive` `a plug-in hybrid vehicle` `first registered` (YMD 2025 2 1) `at` 200000) `under` `D` EQUALS 4100
#ASSERT `monthly` 2026 (`a flat-priced car with drive` `an electric vehicle` `first registered` (YMD 2025 2 1) `at` 200000) `under` `D` EQUALS 3870
-- The reductions are published here for the years of their notes only: (c1), (d1), (d2) for 2026.  A hybrid in 2025 needs a source.
#ASSERT REFUSED `monthly` 2025 (`a vehicle of class` `a car` `, drive` `a hybrid vehicle` `, first registered` (YMD 2025 2 1) `, listed at` 200000 `, daily prices` 0 `over` 365 `days, indices` 105 `and` 100 `, exchange rates` 3.6 `and` 3.6) `under` `D` BECAUSE "the adjusted reduction of the temporary provision is printed (in a Wikisource note) for one tax year only (2024 for regulation 1(b1); 2026 for (c1), (d1) and (d2)): needs a source for other tax years"
-- The period of the temporary provision ends on 31 December 2028: no reduction in 2029 (the cap for 2029 is unpublished, so the whole value is declined).
#ASSERT `the monthly reduction of the temporary provision, on the readings allowed, in the tax year` 2029 `for` (`a flat-priced car with drive` `a hybrid vehicle` `first registered` (YMD 2025 2 1) `at` 200000) `under` `D` EQUALS LIST 0
#ASSERT REFUSED `monthly` 2029 (`a flat-priced car with drive` `an ordinary vehicle` `first registered` (YMD 2025 2 1) `at` 200000) `under` `D` BECAUSE "the cap on the adjusted consumer price is printed (in a Wikisource note) only for 2024, 2025 and 2026: needs a source for other tax years"

-- The adjustment difference (VEH reg 1).  Registered 1 Feb 2025, tax year 2026, index ratio 104 / 100.
GIVEN avgprice IS A NUMBER
      jan      IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A vehicle put at an employee's disposal`
`a car with the average price` avgprice `and the January exchange rate` jan MEANS
    `a vehicle of class` `a car` `, drive` `an ordinary vehicle` `, first registered` (YMD 2025 2 1) `, listed at` 200000 `, daily prices` (avgprice TIMES 365) `over` 365 `days, indices` 104 `and` 100 `, exchange rates` 4.2 `and` jan

-- exchange ratio = 4.2 / 4.0 = 1.05 (not below 1); revalued price 200,000 x 1.05 = 210,000; average 230,000;
--   (1) 230,000 - 210,000 = 20,000;  (2) 230,000 - 200,000 = 30,000;  lower: 20,000, which is 10% of 200,000 (not below 1%)
--   adjusted price 1.04 x (200,000 + 20,000) = 228,800 -> x 2.5% = 5,720 -> 5,720.
#ASSERT `monthly` 2026 (`a car with the average price` 230000 `and the January exchange rate` 4.0) `under` `D` EQUALS 5720
-- exchange ratio = 4.2 / 4.2 = 1; revalued 200,000; average 190,000: (1) max(0, -10,000) = 0; (2) -10,000; lower -10,000, 5% in absolute
--   value -> 1.04 x 190,000 = 197,600 -> x 2.5% = 4,940 -> 4,940.
#ASSERT `monthly` 2026 (`a car with the average price` 190000 `and the January exchange rate` 4.2) `under` `D` EQUALS 4940
-- average 199,000: difference -1,000, 0.5% of the original price, below 1% -> the index ratio times the original price only:
--   1.04 x 200,000 = 208,000 -> 5,200.
#ASSERT `monthly` 2026 (`a car with the average price` 199000 `and the January exchange rate` 4.2) `under` `D` EQUALS 5200
-- average 198,000: difference -2,000, exactly 1% ("נמוך בערכו המוחלט מ־1%": not below) -> the adjustment is used: 1.04 x 198,000 = 205,920
--   -> x 2.5% = 5,148 -> 514.8 tens -> 5,150.
#ASSERT `monthly` 2026 (`a car with the average price` 198000 `and the January exchange rate` 4.2) `under` `D` EQUALS 5150
-- a divisor that is not positive
#ASSERT REFUSED `monthly` 2026 (`a vehicle of class` `a car` `, drive` `an ordinary vehicle` `, first registered` (YMD 2025 2 1) `, listed at` 200000 `, daily prices` 1000 `over` 0 `days, indices` 104 `and` 100 `, exchange rates` 4.2 `and` 4.2) `under` `D` BECAUSE "an input that the adjusted consumer price divides by (the days averaged over, the original price, the index of the year of first registration, or the exchange rate on 1 January) is zero or negative"
-- a vehicle registered after the tax year
#ASSERT REFUSED `monthly` 2024 (`a flat-priced car with drive` `an ordinary vehicle` `first registered` (YMD 2025 2 1) `at` 200000) `under` `D` BECAUSE "the vehicle was first registered after the tax year, so there is no value of its use in it"

§ `Vehicles registered before 2010: the temporary provision reduces the amounts of a repealed schedule`

-- Registered 1 Jun 2008, tax year 2024: average = original (100,000), exchange ratio 1, index ratio 150 / 100 = 1.5:
--   adjusted price 150,000 (adjustment 0, below 1%); x 2.5% = 3,750.  (b1) reduces by 540 in 2024, but "the amounts in the
--   Schedule" no longer exist (the Schedule is repealed): fork SCH.  Reduced: 3,750 - 540 = 3,210; not reduced: 3,750.
`an old hybrid` MEANS `a vehicle of class` `a car` `, drive` `a hybrid vehicle` `, first registered` (YMD 2008 6 1) `, listed at` 100000 `, daily prices` 36500000 `over` 365 `days, indices` 150 `and` 100 `, exchange rates` 3.6 `and` 3.6
#ASSERT REFUSED `monthly` 2024 `an old hybrid` `under` `D` BECAUSE "the monthly value of the use of the vehicle is not settled: the allowed readings (a midpoint in rounding, the personal-import depreciation, the schedule a pre-2010 reduction refers to, a reduction larger than the value) give different amounts"
#ASSERT `monthly` 2024 `an old hybrid` `under` (`the defaults, except old schedule read` `the reduction is taken from the monthly value under regulation 2(a)`) EQUALS 3210
#ASSERT `monthly` 2024 `an old hybrid` `under` (`the defaults, except old schedule read` `no reduction applies to a vehicle registered before 1 January 2010`) EQUALS 3750
-- an old electric vehicle: the provision reduces hybrid vehicles' schedule only; nothing reaches it
#ASSERT `monthly` 2024 (`a vehicle of class` `a car` `, drive` `an electric vehicle` `, first registered` (YMD 2008 6 1) `, listed at` 100000 `, daily prices` 36500000 `over` 365 `days, indices` 150 `and` 100 `, exchange rates` 3.6 `and` 3.6) `under` `D` EQUALS 3750
-- an old plug-in vehicle is a hybrid vehicle (VTP line 17-18): the same fork as the old hybrid
#ASSERT `monthly` 2024 (`a vehicle of class` `a car` `, drive` `a plug-in hybrid vehicle` `, first registered` (YMD 2008 6 1) `, listed at` 100000 `, daily prices` 36500000 `over` 365 `days, indices` 150 `and` 100 `, exchange rates` 3.6 `and` 3.6) `under` (`the defaults, except old schedule read` `the reduction is taken from the monthly value under regulation 2(a)`) EQUALS 3210
-- the reduction under (b1) is published for 2024 only
#ASSERT REFUSED `monthly` 2026 (`a vehicle of class` `a car` `, drive` `a hybrid vehicle` `, first registered` (YMD 2008 6 1) `, listed at` 100000 `, daily prices` 36500000 `over` 365 `days, indices` 150 `and` 100 `, exchange rates` 3.6 `and` 3.6) `under` (`the defaults, except old schedule read` `the reduction is taken from the monthly value under regulation 2(a)`) BECAUSE "the adjusted reduction of the temporary provision is printed (in a Wikisource note) for one tax year only (2024 for regulation 1(b1); 2026 for (c1), (d1) and (d2)): needs a source for other tax years"

§ `A reduction larger than the value`

-- Registered 2026, listed at 20,000: 20,000 x 2.5% = 500.  A hybrid vehicle: (c1) 580 in 2026 -> 500 - 580 = -80.
--   The text does not say what a negative value is (fork XD): nil, or negative.
`a cheap hybrid` MEANS `a flat-priced car with drive` `a hybrid vehicle` `first registered` (YMD 2026 1 5) `at` 20000
#ASSERT REFUSED `monthly` 2026 `a cheap hybrid` `under` `D` BECAUSE "the monthly value of the use of the vehicle is not settled: the allowed readings (a midpoint in rounding, the personal-import depreciation, the schedule a pre-2010 reduction refers to, a reduction larger than the value) give different amounts"
#ASSERT `monthly` 2026 `a cheap hybrid` `under` (`the defaults, except excess deduction read` `the value is then nil`) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `monthly` 2026 `a cheap hybrid` `under` (`the defaults, except excess deduction read` `the value is then negative`) EQUALS (0 MINUS 80)
-- an electric vehicle at the same price: 500 - 1,380 = -880
#ASSERT `monthly` 2026 (`a flat-priced car with drive` `an electric vehicle` `first registered` (YMD 2026 1 5) `at` 20000) `under` (`the defaults, except excess deduction read` `the value is then negative`) EQUALS (0 MINUS 880)

§ `Motorcycles of class L3 (VEH reg 2(b))`

`a motorcycle` MEANS `a vehicle of class` `a motorcycle of class L3` `, drive` `an ordinary vehicle` `, first registered` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, listed at` 30000 `, daily prices` 0 `over` 365 `days, indices` 105 `and` 100 `, exchange rates` 3.6 `and` 3.6
#ASSERT `monthly` 2024 `a motorcycle` `under` `D` EQUALS 1010
#ASSERT `monthly` 2025 `a motorcycle` `under` `D` EQUALS 1040
#ASSERT `monthly` 2026 `a motorcycle` `under` `D` EQUALS 1070
#ASSERT REFUSED `monthly` 2027 `a motorcycle` `under` `D` BECAUSE "the adjusted monthly value of use of an L3 motorcycle is printed (in a Wikisource note) only for 2024, 2025 and 2026: needs a source for other tax years"

§ `A vehicle outside the definition`

-- "רכב" is as defined in the Vehicle Expenses Deduction Regulations of 5755-1995, which are not deposited.
`a thing that is not a vehicle within the 1995 Regulations` MEANS
    `A vehicle put at an employee's disposal` WITH
        `a vehicle within the Vehicle Expenses Deduction Regulations of 5755-1995` IS FALSE
        `the class` IS `a private or light commercial vehicle of class M1 or N1`
        `the drive` IS `an ordinary vehicle`
        `first registered on` IS YMD 2024 3 10
        `the original price` IS `by the importer's price list` WITH `the price on the list, with the standard package, the mandatory accessories and the listed additions, with VAT, without promotion prices and discounts` IS 200000
        `the total of the daily consumer prices in the year of first registration` IS 0
        `the number of days they are averaged over` IS 365
        `the index known on 1 January of the tax year` IS 100
        `the index known on 1 January of the year of first registration` IS 100
        `the average exchange rate of the import currency in the year of first registration` IS 1
        `the exchange rate known on 1 January of the year of first registration` IS 1

#ASSERT REFUSED `monthly` 2024 `a thing that is not a vehicle within the 1995 Regulations` `under` `D` BECAUSE "the Regulations value the use of a 'vehicle' as defined in the Income Tax (Deduction of Vehicle Expenses) Regulations 5755-1995, which are not deposited: needs a source"

§ `A personally imported vehicle (VEH reg 1, "מחיר הרכב לצרכן" (2))`

-- Customs value 100,000; customs 10,000; purchase tax 50,000; VAT 30,000: 190,000 together.  Use depreciation: 1% for each month
-- from the first registration abroad to the import: 12 months -> 12%.  What the percentage is of is not said (fork DEP):
--   of the sum: 190,000 x 12% = 22,800 -> 212,800 -> x 2.5% = 5,320;   of the customs value alone: 12,000 -> 202,000 -> 5,050.
GIVEN months IS A NUMBER
      part   IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A vehicle put at an employee's disposal`
`a car imported with 12 months of depreciation: whole months` months `, a part of a month remained:` part MEANS
    `A vehicle put at an employee's disposal` WITH
        `a vehicle within the Vehicle Expenses Deduction Regulations of 5755-1995` IS TRUE
        `the class` IS `a private or light commercial vehicle of class M1 or N1`
        `the drive` IS `an ordinary vehicle`
        `first registered on` IS YMD 2024 3 10
        `the original price` IS `by personal import with no parallel commercial import` WITH
            `the value fixed for customs` IS 100000,
            `the customs duty payable, or that would be but for exemptions` IS 10000,
            `the purchase tax payable, or that would be but for exemptions` IS 50000,
            `the VAT payable, or that would be but for exemptions` IS 30000,
            `whole months from first registration abroad to import` IS months,
            `a part of a month remained` IS part
        `the total of the daily consumer prices in the year of first registration` IS 0
        `the number of days they are averaged over` IS 365
        `the index known on 1 January of the tax year` IS 100
        `the index known on 1 January of the year of first registration` IS 100
        `the average exchange rate of the import currency in the year of first registration` IS 1
        `the exchange rate known on 1 January of the year of first registration` IS 1

#ASSERT REFUSED `monthly` 2024 (`a car imported with 12 months of depreciation: whole months` 12 `, a part of a month remained:` FALSE) `under` `D` BECAUSE "the monthly value of the use of the vehicle is not settled: the allowed readings (a midpoint in rounding, the personal-import depreciation, the schedule a pre-2010 reduction refers to, a reduction larger than the value) give different amounts"
#ASSERT `monthly` 2024 (`a car imported with 12 months of depreciation: whole months` 12 `, a part of a month remained:` FALSE) `under` (`the defaults, except depreciation base read` `one per cent of the sum of the customs value, customs, purchase tax and VAT` `and part month of depreciation read` `a part of a month does not count`) EQUALS 5320
#ASSERT `monthly` 2024 (`a car imported with 12 months of depreciation: whole months` 12 `, a part of a month remained:` FALSE) `under` (`the defaults, except depreciation base read` `one per cent of the customs value alone` `and part month of depreciation read` `a part of a month does not count`) EQUALS 5050
-- A part of a month left over: 12 months and a part.  On the sum: counted as a month, 13% x 190,000 = 24,700 -> 214,700 -> x 2.5% = 5,367.5 -> 536.75 tens -> 5,370;
--   not counted, 12% -> 5,320.
#ASSERT `monthly` 2024 (`a car imported with 12 months of depreciation: whole months` 12 `, a part of a month remained:` TRUE) `under` (`the defaults, except depreciation base read` `one per cent of the sum of the customs value, customs, purchase tax and VAT` `and part month of depreciation read` `a part of a month counts as a month of depreciation`) EQUALS 5370
#ASSERT `monthly` 2024 (`a car imported with 12 months of depreciation: whole months` 12 `, a part of a month remained:` TRUE) `under` (`the defaults, except depreciation base read` `one per cent of the sum of the customs value, customs, purchase tax and VAT` `and part month of depreciation read` `a part of a month does not count`) EQUALS 5320

§ `A vehicle for part of a tax year`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
      c IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The use of a vehicle in a tax year`
`the use for` a `whole months and` b `days of a month of` c `days` MEANS
    `The use of a vehicle in a tax year` WITH
        `whole months it was at the employee's disposal` IS a
        `days of a further part of a month` IS b
        `days in that month` IS c

-- The Regulations fix the value "לכל חודש" (for each month).  Twelve whole months at 5,250: 63,000.
#ASSERT `the value for the tax year, from the monthly value` 5250 `, for` (`the use for` 12 `whole months and` 0 `days of a month of` 31 `days`) `, under` `D` EQUALS 63000
-- 6 months and 10 days of a 30-day month: counted as a month -> 7 x 5,250 = 36,750; prorated -> (6 + 10/30) = 19/3 x 5,250 = 33,250;
--   not counted -> 6 x 5,250 = 31,500.  The text does not say (fork PM): declined by default.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the value for the tax year, from the monthly value` 5250 `, for` (`the use for` 6 `whole months and` 10 `days of a month of` 30 `days`) `, under` `D` BECAUSE "the months to count are not settled: the Regulations fix a value for each month and do not say whether a part of a month counts as a month, is prorated by days, or does not count"
#ASSERT `the value for the tax year, from the monthly value` 5250 `, for` (`the use for` 6 `whole months and` 10 `days of a month of` 30 `days`) `, under` (`the defaults, except part month read` `a part of a month counts as a month`) EQUALS 36750
#ASSERT `the value for the tax year, from the monthly value` 5250 `, for` (`the use for` 6 `whole months and` 10 `days of a month of` 30 `days`) `, under` (`the defaults, except part month read` `a part of a month is prorated by days`) EQUALS 33250
#ASSERT `the value for the tax year, from the monthly value` 5250 `, for` (`the use for` 6 `whole months and` 10 `days of a month of` 30 `days`) `, under` (`the defaults, except part month read` `a part of a month does not count`) EQUALS 31500
-- more than twelve months in all; a further part as long as the month itself
#ASSERT REFUSED `the value for the tax year, from the monthly value` 5250 `, for` (`the use for` 12 `whole months and` 5 `days of a month of` 31 `days`) `, under` `D` BECAUSE "the months of use given are negative or over twelve, or the days of the further part of a month are negative or not fewer than the days in that month"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the value for the tax year, from the monthly value` 5250 `, for` (`the use for` 5 `whole months and` 31 `days of a month of` 31 `days`) `, under` `D` BECAUSE "the months of use given are negative or over twelve, or the days of the further part of a month are negative or not fewer than the days in that month"

§ `A mobile telephone (TEL reg 2)`

GIVEN workplace IS A BOOLEAN
      expense   IS A NUMBER
      paid      IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A mobile telephone put at an employee's disposal`
`a telephone, workplace calls only:` workplace `, monthly expense` expense `, paid by the employee` paid MEANS
    `A mobile telephone put at an employee's disposal` WITH
        `a telephone from which calls can be made to the place of work only` IS workplace
        `the monthly expense` IS expense
        `the part of the monthly expense the employee paid` IS paid

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      p IS A `A mobile telephone put at an employee's disposal`
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-29`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`phone` y p `under` r MEANS `s 2(2)(b) — the monthly value of the use of a mobile telephone in the tax year` y `, of` p `under` r

-- The lower of half the monthly expense and NIS 115 (2023 to 2027), less what the employee paid.
--   expense 200: half 100 < 115 -> 100;   expense 300: half 150 -> 115;  paid 20 -> 95.
--   expense 230: half 115 = 115 -> 115;  expense 232: half 116 -> 115.
#ASSERT `phone` 2026 (`a telephone, workplace calls only:` FALSE `, monthly expense` 200 `, paid by the employee` 0) `under` `D` EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `phone` 2026 (`a telephone, workplace calls only:` FALSE `, monthly expense` 300 `, paid by the employee` 20) `under` `D` EQUALS 95
#ASSERT `phone` 2026 (`a telephone, workplace calls only:` FALSE `, monthly expense` 230 `, paid by the employee` 0) `under` `D` EQUALS 115
#ASSERT `phone` 2026 (`a telephone, workplace calls only:` FALSE `, monthly expense` 232 `, paid by the employee` 0) `under` `D` EQUALS 115
#ASSERT `phone` 2024 (`a telephone, workplace calls only:` FALSE `, monthly expense` 400 `, paid by the employee` 0) `under` `D` EQUALS 115
#ASSERT `phone` 2027 (`a telephone, workplace calls only:` FALSE `, monthly expense` 400 `, paid by the employee` 0) `under` `D` EQUALS 115
-- The published ceiling runs to 2027; 2028 needs a source.  Before 2024 the row holds no text.
#ASSERT REFUSED `phone` 2028 (`a telephone, workplace calls only:` FALSE `, monthly expense` 400 `, paid by the employee` 0) `under` `D` BECAUSE "the adjusted ceiling of the monthly value of use of a mobile telephone is printed (in a Wikisource note) only for 2019 to 2027: needs a source for other tax years"
#ASSERT REFUSED `phone` 2023 (`a telephone, workplace calls only:` FALSE `, monthly expense` 400 `, paid by the employee` 0) `under` `D` BECAUSE "row IL-29 does not hold the text of these provisions for a tax year before 2024"
-- A telephone from which only the workplace can be called is outside the Regulations' value.
#ASSERT REFUSED `phone` 2026 (`a telephone, workplace calls only:` TRUE `, monthly expense` 200 `, paid by the employee` 0) `under` `D` BECAUSE "the Regulations fix no value for a mobile telephone from which calls can be made to the place of work only, and s 2(2)(b) fixes none otherwise: the text does not say what its use is worth"
-- The employee paid more than the value: expense 200 -> value 100; he paid 120 of it -> -20 (nil, or negative: fork XD).
#ASSERT REFUSED `phone` 2026 (`a telephone, workplace calls only:` FALSE `, monthly expense` 200 `, paid by the employee` 120) `under` `D` BECAUSE "the monthly value of the use of the telephone is not settled: the Regulations do not say what the value is where the employee paid more than the value (nil, or negative)"
#ASSERT `phone` 2026 (`a telephone, workplace calls only:` FALSE `, monthly expense` 200 `, paid by the employee` 120) `under` (`the defaults, except excess deduction read` `the value is then nil`) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `phone` 2026 (`a telephone, workplace calls only:` FALSE `, monthly expense` 200 `, paid by the employee` 120) `under` (`the defaults, except excess deduction read` `the value is then negative`) EQUALS (0 MINUS 20)
-- paid exactly the value: 100 - 100 = 0, not below zero: answers on every reading.
#ASSERT `phone` 2026 (`a telephone, workplace calls only:` FALSE `, monthly expense` 200 `, paid by the employee` 100) `under` `D` EQUALS 0
-- the employee cannot have paid more than the whole expense
#ASSERT REFUSED `phone` 2026 (`a telephone, workplace calls only:` FALSE `, monthly expense` 200 `, paid by the employee` 201) `under` `D` BECAUSE "the part of the monthly expense the employee paid is negative or exceeds the monthly expense"
